.TH USB-UPDATE 8 "2026-08-18" "usb-update __VERSION__" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
usb-update \- update the TwinCAT boot folder and TwinCAT HMI project on a
Beckhoff RT Linux device from a USB stick at boot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-update
runs at every boot, before the TwinCAT runtime and the TwinCAT HMI (TF2000)
server start.
If a USB stick with the configured volume label (default
.BR UPDATE )
carries a package that is not already installed, an
.B Update / Skip
dialog is shown on the HMI; the HMI browser is held back until the operator
answers.
An unanswered dialog times out to Skip, so an unattended power cycle never
hangs the machine.
.PP
On
.BR Update ,
the current state is backed up, the new files are staged and verified, then
swapped in.
Device state (event logs, PLC persistent data) is carried over from the
machine, never taken from the stick.
After TwinCAT starts, a second service validates that it reached RUN (and,
on HMI machines, that the HMI server answers).
On success the rollback copy is removed; on failure the operator is offered
a revert to the previous working version.
.PP
A stick whose package is already installed is ignored, so a stick left in
the port is harmless.
An empty file named
.B RESTORE
at the root of a labeled stick offers restoring the last backup instead.
.SH OPERATION
Insert the prepared stick, power-cycle the machine, answer the dialog,
remove the stick.
The stick layout and preparation steps are described in the README (see
.BR "SEE ALSO" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/usb-update/usb-update.conf
Configuration; every tunable is documented in the file.
Preserved across package upgrades.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/usb-update/
The scripts, each self-documented, orchestrated by
.B usb-update.service
(boot-time check and apply) and
.B usb-update-validate.service
(post-boot validation).
.TP
.I /var/lib/usb-update/
State: backups and the installed-package id.
Kept on package removal, deleted on purge.
.SH LOGGING
Everything logs to the persistent journal under one tag:
.PP
.nf
    journalctl -t usb-update -b
.fi
.PP
.B validate: SUCCESS
is the happy ending;
.B validate: FAILURE
includes TwinCAT's own error lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and releases:
.I https://github.com/Beckhoff-USA-Community/USB-Boot-Folder-Update-for-Beckhoff-RT-Linux
.PP
Not an official Beckhoff tool.
